Date: Tue, 23 Jun 2026 06:22:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/15] Volume Landmarks (#12): weekly sets per muscle vs
 optimal range

Counts weekly working sets per muscle group from existing session data and
compares against evidence-based optimal ranges (MEV-MRV style). Pure,
deterministic; no schema change.

- domain/volume/VolumeLandmarks.kt: maps fine-grained library muscles to
  10 trainable groups; counts working sets (warmups excluded), primary x1.0
  + secondary x0.5 fractional accounting; status Under/In Range/Above/None.
- TrainingDnaViewModel: computes volumeLandmarks from completed sessions
  (1-week window) and exposes them in state.
- Training DNA screen: 'Weekly volume' section with a card per trained
  muscle group (sets/week, optimal range, status, progress bar).

Verified: domain compiles on kotlinc 1.9.22 (170 classes); 4 logic tests
pass in-sandbox (in-range, fractional secondary, warmup exclusion, above/
none). No tests committed.
